#EXTINF:2281 group-title="Non Fiction Social Science (Culture & Anthropology)",The Golden Bough Part 2 — James Frazer · VI — TABOOED WORDS. PART 3. 4. Names of Kings and other Sacred Persons tabooed. Birthnames of kings tabooed- Names of Zulu chiefs and kings tabooed- Names of living kings and chiefs tabooed in Madagascar- Names of dead kings and chiefs tabooed in Madagascar- Names of chiefs tabooed in Polynesia- Names of Eleusinian priests tabooed- Names of members of the Yewe order in Togo tabooed- The utterance of the names of gods and spirit supposed to disturb the course of nature- Winter and summer names of the Kwakiutl Indians. 5. Names of Gods tabooed. Names of gods kept secret- Ra and Isis- Divine names used to conjure with by wizards in Egypt- North Africa- and China- Divine names used by the Romans to conjure with- Taboos on the names of kings and commoners alike in origin. - Read by Leon Harvey - Duration 00:38:01
